sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila melanogaster Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.736 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion on an 8-by-6-wavelength periodic patch. Gamma is solved so the analytic critical wavelength of D. melanogaster is 2.736 µm (2.736e-06 m, log10=-5.563, tier 3_subcellular_um). At that same gamma, reconstructed wavelengths are 2.242 µm (D. miranda, successor) and 3.243 µm (D. mauritiana, predecessor), all at 0 Ma. Numerical dispersion Pearson r = 0.9999999989, RMSE = 4.62e-5. Nonlinear FFT wavelength is 2.799 µm (2.3% longer than the linear target). Equal-diffusion ablation std is 7.8e-5 against a patterned std of 0.117. The growth GIF is 16 frames at 768x576; its last frame is the Karwath male with activator darkening at amplitude 0.16 and scores CV similarity 96.0 against that photograph. Overall 86.2/100 (faithfulness 86.0, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-melanogaster-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 422992 B, 1488×1104 px, artifact_sha256 a5198e44d82533312ce2e385854f8ba7c3d9601826b8b99d7df8ea883615039b (sha256 a5198e44d82533312ce2e385854f8ba7c3d9601826b8b99d7df8ea883615039b), spec_fingerprint 995c7441a1e86dd55fbe8e523c9fea39052280d57b46ba75e4b98b1e0c116683. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 995c7441a1e86dd55fbe8e523c9fea39052280d57b46ba75e4b98b1e0c116683; artifact_sha256: a5198e44d82533312ce2e385854f8ba7c3d9601826b8b99d7df8ea883615039b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_melanogaster_specimen.jpg=2a66a100d8405cc9..., datasets/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_melanogaster_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=553df65dcc62824e...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite wavelength by diffusion-driven instability. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics are f = a - u + u^2 v and g = b - u^2 v. | Wittkopp, True and Carroll (2002) place Drosophila melanin via Yellow and Ebony. | True et al. (1997) quantify morphological divergence of D. mauritiana from the simulans complex. | Richards et al. (2005) compare the D. pseudoobscura genome with D. melanogaster. | The Karwath photograph is an adult male D. melanogaster under CC BY-SA 2.5.; reconstructed_in_script: Gamma = 1.032078 is solved so argmax sigma(k) = 2 pi / 2.736 per micrometre. | Mauritiana (a=0.16, b=0.72, Du=0.055, Dv=1.15) and miranda (a=0.07, b=1.25, Du=0.020, Dv=2.20) wavelengths at that shared gamma. | Explicit-Euler periodic integration, radial-FFT wavelength, and eigenvector growth-rate correlation. | Registration of the steady activator onto the photograph at amplitude 0.16.; transfer_boundary: 2.736 µm is the assigned detail scale for this slot, not a published melanin-granule spacing. | Chronospecies wavelengths are reconstructions. True 1997 and Richards 2005 do not report these micrometre values. | Richards 2005 sequenced D. pseudoobscura. D. miranda is in that obscura clade; the paper is not a miranda pigment micrograph.; does_not_claim: That adult abdominal stripes or ommatidia have wavelength 2.736 µm. | That the spot lattice is a photograph of an ocellus. | That a near-unit dispersion correlation validates the nonlinear field against an electron micrograph. | A second independent assessor.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=1.8]: Chronospecies wavelengths are linear k_c only; confirm after nonlinear saturation.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/morphometric-validation, pressure P=1.3]: Single luminance quantile for the specimen mask; sweep it.",
            "remediation needed: Integrate a saturated 1D Schnakenberg field for mauritiana and miranda and check that the nonlinear wavelengths keep the linear order miranda < melanogaster < mauritiana.",
            "remediation needed: Sweep the specimen foreground luminance quantile (currently 0.70) and report whether foreground fraction and circularity stay stable." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.862"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent cloud loop; no second provider)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

